  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Hello, here is my feedback on the third-person beta:\n\nF5 as the default toggle feels out of place, since it’s widely used for refresh/reload in browsers, Windows Explorer, and even some world content (e.g., ProTV). A different default key would avoid conflicts with some existing content.\n\nDesktop item holding: the usual scroll functionality is lost unless Alt is pressed. I suggest keeping scroll as-is, and using \"ALT + SCROLL\" to trigger third person. When the camera is adjusted, movement keys (WASD) should remain relative to the character, not force rotation toward a direction.\n\nCamera controls: holding down \"Alt\" while in third person using the mouse could serve as an alternate easy way for moving the camera (instead of the hard switch with Tab).  \n\n   + \"SHIFT + ALT + SCROLL WHEEL\" could handle vertical camera movement.  \n\n   + \"ALT + MIDDLE MOUSE\" could adjust view angles/shoulder perspective.\n\nI understand these bindings won’t suit everyone, but since interaction prompts are already included, they could help guide users through new alternative controls without confusion, better I say something than nothing I suppose.",
